commit.message:
Renamed the AbstractMonitoringReader;
Modified the meta model;
Added the methods in question to the ports and the plugins.

Modified the meta-model and re-generated the java-files;
Corrected some parts of the plugins to suit the new port-structure;
Modified the Analysis-Controller in order to provide two additional constructors to initialize the analysis based on a model-instance;
Theoretically the analysis with a model-instance is runnable again, but the init-string for the reader is not used currently.

set analysis to Java 1.8;
fixed TestTimestampFilter;
there are still some syntax errors left

refactored build.gradle to use a shared manifest for all three jar
targets;
fixed bridge dependency;
fixed kax-files dependency

finished BinaryLogReader;
refactored tests;
fixed ExplorViz test

Corrected the wiring within the TraceAnalysisTool;
Made sure that some of the plugins get now the correct input+output;
Extended the port-test-case.

Removed the obsolete "IMonitoringRecordConsumerPlugin"-interface;
Started with the serialize-method of the AnalysisController;
Replaced at some points the "IMonitoringRecordConsumerPlugin" with "AbstractAnalysisPlugin";
Continued the modification of the plugins.

removed duplicated, old jetty libs;
fixed FSUtil;
fixed some tests

Modified the meta model for the analysis;
Modified the example for this new model;
Regenerated the classes for this model;
Modified some parts of the project in order to ensure that one can use the example file.

removed jmx reader and associated integration test;
added package-info files for legacy packages;
fixed raw type warnings in PlotStep

Corrected a case in the FSReader;
Added some comments;
Implemented the configuration of some plugins

fixed bug in rolling file algorithm of BinaryFileWriterPool and
AsciiFileWriterPool;
fixed many tests by declaring properties in kieker.properties

removed old writers;
refactored filesystem writers and their tests;
fixed some remaining syntax errors

changed JRE from 1.6 to 1.7 for all gradle modules;
fixed concurrency issues in tests;
removed groupby from Flow.irl as Eclipse workaround;
added unresolved libraries to the classpath of the individual Eclipse
projects

added findbugs 3.* to Eclipse classpath to use SuppressFBWarnings;
fixed gradle function "htmlQualityReport": it now generates reports for
main and test for all projects

added WriterUtil;
finished BinaryFileWriter;
finished AsciiFileWriter

record factory implementation in TCPReader ready for testing;
implementation falls back to a RecordFactory wrapper that calls
AbstractMonitoringRecord.create()

Added a new testcase to test the output port;
Fixed a bug within the output port;
Made sure that the TraceReconstructionFilter gets now the correct objects.

removed gradle nature;
removed eclipse plugin since it does not produce the Eclipse
configurations which we want to have

fixed bug in BlockingQueueDecorator;
added WriterControllerTest;
added Mockito as test dependency

made CachedRecordFactoryCatalog singleton;
RecordFactoryResolver now returns null on exception;
further minor issues discussed in dev meeting

fixed ExplorVizReader;
removed tests for DbReader;
made IPipeWriter obsolete

Made sure that the FSReader does have static output classes again;
Added some tests;
Added some comments;
Corrected the ExecutionRecordTransformationFilter to suit the analysis tool again

KIEKER-1521 fixed;
removed obsolete writer configuration options in
kieker.monitoring.default.properties

Moved the new exception class to the correct subfolder;
Implemented some of the methods for the plugins;
Solved the problem with the "FilesystemLogReplayer";
Made the project compilable again.
